        "subject": "LU-9633 obdclass: fix up md_attrs.c kernel doc",
        "message": "LU-9633 obdclass: fix up md_attrs.c kernel doc\n\nThe kernel doc conversion of lustre/obdclass/md_attrs.c left\nlustre_loa_init() as the only function in the file without a doc\nblock; add one describing @loa, @fid, @compat and @incompat.\n\nNone of these structures are MDT-only, so drop the wording that\nsays they are.  lustre_lma_init() is called on OST objects as\nwell - osd-zfs adds LMAC_FID_ON_OST in osd_create() and\nosd_obj_create() - and lustre_loa_init() is used for MDT-side\ninodes such as agent inodes and OI files via osd_ea_fid_set(),\nso both blocks now describe @compat and @incompat as\nLMAC_*/LMAI_* rather than as things \"MDS\" understands.  For the\nsame reason \"(for OST-object only)\" is dropped from\nlustre_loa_swab(), which osd_get_lma() calls for every ldiskfs\ninode; that summary's grammar is fixed while it is touched.\n\nThe new Return: section of lustre_buf2hsm() listed only success\nand generic failure, but -ENODATA is a normal outcome meaning\nthe object carries no HSM xattr, and the callers that check the\nreturn value handle it as such rather than as an error\n(mdt_attr_get_complex(), mdd_hsm_update_locked() and\nmdd_hsm_archive_exists()).  Document it separately from real\nerrors, and note in @rc that the value passed in may itself be\na negative errno.\n\nA \"featores\" typo in the lustre_lma_init() doc block is fixed\ntoo.\n\nComment-only change, no functional change.\n\nFixes: 7d900dee052f (\"LU-9633 obdclass: Add kernel doc style for obdclass (13)\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Iab1ab3ed2a08819491542c2f31c4ef58839137d2\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68171\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
